I ascended my barb (first ascension) without casting a single spell. I
rather like the fact that you could cast spells while being a barbarian
however. Making spells useless for a class, any one, is bad imho
because you end up with lots of spellbooks that are useless. NetHack
doesn't have that many useless objects, but it would have, and it would
be a bad move in my opinion. If you want a non spellcasting barb, you
can play one very easily.
Your lock proposal I don't like either, nor any of the free hand stuff.
Adding new capabilities like using herbs for healing I like. What herb?
A new kind of comsetible that is useful for all classes (as nourishing
as garlic for example) but that healers/cavemen can apply would be
good.
Barbs could get a #fastattack instead of #twoweapon that is useable
only with two-handed weapons and does something along the same lines
(two attacks but at -X/-X).
You could put a specific penalty on healers for killing one of their
kind (that's Hippocrates' oath after all). It should at least abuse the
healer's wisdom. Or worse (particularly funny when dealing with humans
on the astral plane).
Rogues should really be able to #rob another character (like a
shopkeeper) in order to steal some of their equipment, a bit like
nymphs' or leprechauns' attacks, except the target should be peaceful,
and if the attack fails, target is no longer peaceful.
A class-specific item, like the cornuthaum, would generally be a good
thing. Unless quite powerful, they may not change the end-game, though.
But still. Things like a barbarian armor which would give an AC bonus
only to barbs.


